{
  "id": "ss.fx.acidpool",
  "name": "Acid pool",
  "description": "The pool Caustic Trail leaves where an acid glob spends itself: an irregular puddle, fourteen lumpy vertices between r=22 and r=30 — thirty is the number the game scales by, as it does the barb burst — with a body that runs bile at the middle out to venom-dark at the edge because the middle is where it is burning, a paler sheen across it, five hollow bubbles of three sizes and two solid beads. Two things were added once the trail was seen laid rather than looked at one pool at a time. A scorch ring outside the rim, ground eaten black, which is what acid does to a floor and is also what keeps two pools apart: a glob spends itself where the last one did often enough that three of these overlap, and before the scorch they merged into one green mass with no telling how many globs had died there. And three pits bitten through the body, dark holes rather than more highlights, because every other mark on this document was lighter than what it sat on and a puddle made only of highlights reads as jelly rather than as something eating. No frost and no magenta: this is the player's weapon, but it is acid rather than cold, so it borrows the glob's own greens and nothing else's. The canvas is 80 for the same reason the blast's is — the spread at full scale lands on a 64 boundary.",
