    "play": {
      "description": "Three quarters of a second, the pool's life. The puddle spreads out to size in the first fifth and then just sits; what moves after that is the acid working — bubbles rising one after another, each swelling to a pop and gone, the two beads bobbing, the sheen drifting, and the three pits opening a little wider as they eat down. The scorch arrives ahead of the puddle rather than with it, because the ground is bitten the instant the glob lands and the pool only then settles into the hole. The fade out belongs to the game, which is already scaling the sprite's alpha by how much life the pool has left.",
